00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:58,077
Plus, the tiny veins in your eyes
will snap and you'll go blind.

254
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:01,101
You can go ahead and
accelerate time all you want.

255
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:04,317
Weather forecast is a stand
that can control the weather.

256
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:08,597
I already used it to accumulate a massive
amount of pure oxygen into this room.

257
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:11,151
And now, you'll slowly lose consciousness,

258
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:14,740
as 100 % oxygen seeps deeper
and deeper into your tissues.

259
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:18,340
No, I refuse to let a
branch like you beat me!

260
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:20,537
I'm not the one in control here.

261
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:23,091
This is Weather Forecast's hidden ability.

262
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,337
You're the one who stole Weather's memory?

263
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:26,917
and the one who awakened him again!

264
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,059
when he regained his power
to project killer snails.

265
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:33,020
Father Poochie, it was all because of you.

266
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:36,060
Gravity still affects you, too.

267
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:39,020
You are unable to defeat your destiny.

268
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:44,880
No, you have to end this, Emporial.

269
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:46,677
You can still stop Weather.

270
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:48,477
Do not let him do this.

271
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:52,260
After I finally attained the
ability I've worked so hard for,

272
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:54,000
God wished it to be so!

273
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:57,240
It was an ability that God
chose for me to possess!

274
00:15:57,480 --> 00:16:02,186
A new history of humanity will be born,
and the future of mankind will be saved!

275
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:04,517
We haven't even reached
the point in time yet

276
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:07,541
where time acceleration
started in Cape Canaveral.

277
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:10,055
Maiden Heaven has yet to be completed.

278
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:14,357
As long as it's after Cape Canaveral,
I will gladly sacrifice my life.

279
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:15,680
But if I die now,

280
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:19,637
I don't mean that everything I've done thus
far will have been utterly meaningless.

281
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:22,602
The fate of all humanity
will be changed forever.

282
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:27,037
If i die, people won't be able to see
their future as it happens before them?

283
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:29,497
which means they won't be
able to face their fate.

284
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:30,698
Don't you remember?

285
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:33,417
Accepting their fate is
how they'll be truly happy.

286
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:35,997
It was my mission to bring
about true happiness.

287
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:37,580
I cannot die here.

288
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:39,820
Don't you understand?

289
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:42,700
Fate won, and you are the loser.

290
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,660
You insignificant little.

291
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,217
I didn't do this alone.

292
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:50,771
Jolene knew I'd make it here, and this
is what she would've wanted me to do.

293
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:56,480
Brother 2, and FF, Ermes,
Anastasia, and even Mr. Jotaro.

294
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:01,505
We had no idea what the future
held, but we all had resolutions.

295
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:05,409
The one who couldn't accept
their own fate was you, Poochie.

296
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:08,666
True fate is walking
down the path of justice.

297
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:09,800
You're done for!

298
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:11,420
No, I'm not!

299
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:15,225
You're the one who doesn't
understand anything!

300
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:20,831
Go to hell, you insignificant little brat!

301
00:17:56,340 --> 00:18:02,480
Oh, my God.

302
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:26,470
The bus

303
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:32,900
Give me a break I already told
you I've only got this 50 on me

304
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:36,068
Why don't you carry
change on the bus anyway

305
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:42,977
You're for real You gotta top
down Fine fine just hold up a sec

306
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:46,942
would ya I'm gonna go break this
50 at that gas station real quick

307
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:49,336
Oh, hey kid, you gettin' on this bus?

308
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:51,049
Talk about perfect timing.

309
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:52,578
You got any change?

310
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:54,460
I need to break this 50.

311
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,030
Yeah?

312
00:18:56,113 --> 00:18:56,977
Is that good with you?

313
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:59,001
It ain't a counterfeit, trust me.

314
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:00,350
What the?

315
00:19:00,433 --> 00:19:02,000
Don't leave me, dumbass!

316
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:04,017
Ah, just throw it back like that!

317
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:04,930
Hey!

318
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:07,090
Come on!

319
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:10,957
The bus went and drove off because your
response time was so freakin' slow!

320
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:13,097
I'm gonna wait two hours for the next one.

321
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:14,057
What the hell, man?

322
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:14,970
Ben!

323
00:19:15,053 --> 00:19:16,246
Are you even listening to me?

324
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:17,590
Damn it.

325
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,475
Yeah, well, whatever.

326
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:23,457
That cheap prick probably thought I was a
fugitive from Green Dolphin or something.

327
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:24,370
You...

328
00:19:24,453 --> 00:19:25,283
you are?

329
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:26,730
Huh?

330
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:29,210
Hey.

331
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,900
My car completely ran out of gas.

332
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:34,217
If you hook us up with some
gas and food with that 50,

333
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:37,337
I'll let you catch a ride
to wherever you want to go.

334
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:38,780
Same goes for you, kid.

335
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:42,057
Is that how you save on
travel expenses or something?

336
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:46,905
My sister used to always tell me to never
get in a car with some random stranger.

337
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:56,017
There's a storm on the way
too bad have fun getting

338
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:58,777
drenched while you wait
for the next bus to come!

339
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:01,625
But I don't think it's
letting up anytime soon.

340
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,420
Hop on in, kiddo.

341
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:12,682
It's okay, we're not bad people.

342
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:18,180
Call me Irene, and this
guy here is Anikis.

343
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,621
Where's your mom and dad at, bud?

344
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:24,466
We were actually just on our way
to visit my old man right now.

345
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:27,250
You see?

346
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,280
He's my boyfriend.

347
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:36,437
I don't know how things will turn out,
but if Dad approves of us being together,

348
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:39,300
then maybe we'll even get married.

349
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:42,700
Shit, man.

350
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:44,917
Is there really a storm heading this way?

351
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,997
I'll ride along, but ten bucks
is all you're getting from me.

352
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:51,357
I'm gonna have you guys make a
stop at Cape Canaveral, too, okay?

353
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:52,597
Come on, get in here.

354
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,445
We could really use your help.

355
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:56,560
Yeah, me too. To be honest.

356
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:59,261
You doing okay there, little boy?

357
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,460
Can you tell me your name?

358
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:07,320
Come on, I said to get in.

359
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:13,573
And I don't expect you to pay us either.

360
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:15,948
You're shaking like a tree.

361
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,600
Are you cold?

362
00:21:18,460 --> 00:21:19,290
Here.

363
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:23,930
Emporio.

364
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:27,850
Emporio.

365
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:36,340
That's what you can call me, since
you wanted to know my name's Emporio.

366
00:21:49,380 --> 00:21:51,660
Hey, look, there's a hitchhiker.

367
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:54,136
I'm not picking up another straggler.

368
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:55,617
Two is more than enough.

369
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:58,317
You're the one that said
there's a storm coming.

370
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:00,694
Come on, stop the car for the poor guy.

371
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:25,937
I'll be the roundabout.

372
00:22:26,020 --> 00:22:30,097
The words will make you out and out.

373
00:22:30,180 --> 00:22:33,400
And spend the day your way.

374
00:22:35,300 --> 00:22:38,197
Call it morning driving through the sun.

375
00:22:38,280 --> 00:22:39,880
And in and out the valley.

376
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:52,977
The music dance and sing.

377
00:22:53,060 --> 00:22:57,137
They make the children really ring.

378
00:22:57,220 --> 00:23:01,380
I spend the day your way.

379
00:23:02,540 --> 00:23:05,337
Cold and morning driving through the sun.

380
00:23:05,420 --> 00:23:07,140
And in and out the valley.

381
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:11,780
In and out around the lake.

382
00:23:12,860 --> 00:23:15,197
Mountains come out of the sky.

383
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:16,940
And they stand there.

384
00:23:19,980 --> 00:23:23,660
When my lover will be
there and we'll see you.

385
00:23:26,420 --> 00:23:30,060
Ten and two summers will
be there laughing too.

386
00:23:32,980 --> 00:23:35,737
Twenty and four before my lover will see.

387
00:23:35,820 --> 00:23:38,760
I'll be there with you.

388
00:24:16,940 --> 00:24:21,760
Thank you.
